From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:22:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: finish tx-free processing on a truncated
 event

When mt7915_mac_tx_free() ran past the end of the event it returned
straight away. The tokens it had already released had their skbs queued
on free_list, so they were never freed, and a pending tx wake-up was
lost; if those were the last outstanding tokens, tx stayed blocked.
The fixed header was also read without checking the event's length.

Check the header length, make sure a whole entry fits before reading
it, and stop the loop instead of returning so the completion runs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mt7915/mac.c | 11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mt7915/mac.c b/mt7915/mac.c
index c3054e0c..8489f015 100644
--- a/mt7915/mac.c
+++ b/mt7915/mac.c
@@ -876,11 +876,15 @@ mt7915_mac_tx_free(struct mt7915_dev *dev, void *data, int len)
 	void *end = data + len;
 	bool v3, wake = false;
 	u16 total, count = 0;
-	u32 txd = le32_to_cpu(free->txd);
 	__le32 *cur_info;
+	u32 txd;
+
+	if (WARN_ON_ONCE(len < sizeof(*free)))
+		return;
 
 	mt7915_mac_tx_free_prepare(dev);
 
+	txd = le32_to_cpu(free->txd);
 	total = le16_get_bits(free->ctrl, MT_TX_FREE_MSDU_CNT);
 	v3 = (FIELD_GET(MT_TX_FREE_VER, txd) == 0x4);
 
@@ -888,8 +892,9 @@ mt7915_mac_tx_free(struct mt7915_dev *dev, void *data, int len)
 		u32 msdu, info;
 		u8 i;
 
-		if (WARN_ON_ONCE((void *)cur_info >= end))
-			return;
+		/* tokens released so far sit on free_list: always finish */
+		if (WARN_ON_ONCE((void *)(cur_info + 1) > end))
+			break;
 
 		/*
 		 * 1'b1: new wcid pair.
